laim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Parent epic 1386 was remediated — read before implementing\n\nThe epic's AC1 was UNSATISFIABLE as written (it banned all SC vocabulary under `src/rebar/`\nwhile its own Scope deferred some) and has been amended. This does not change your scope, but\nit fixes what \"done\" means for the epic, and it names carve-outs you must NOT \"fix\":\n\n**Four permanent vocabulary carve-outs** — leave these exactly as they are:\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T2.md` — \"a pilot with metrics, or stated success\n  criteria for a trial\". Generic English about an EXPERIMENT succeeding, not the ticket\n  heading. Story 2aa6's AC6 REQUIRES it to survive.\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier.md`,\n  `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier_agentic.md`, and the `dod_uncertifiable` field\n  description in `src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify_models.py` — the\n  `dod_uncertifiable` / \"definition-of-done\" concept, which this epic explicitly defers.\n\n**Also amended:** epic AC5 now pins `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` at EXACTLY ONE SC\nmatch (T2's echo) rather than zero — the guide is GENERATED from the criteria registry and\nembeds each criterion's prompt verbatim, so zero was impossible.\n\n**A gap was found and assigned to 5f4d, not to you:** `src/rebar/llm/completion.py:288`\n(\"its success criteria are met across children\") is genuine heading-sense vocabulary that no\nstory owned. It is now in 5f4d's scope. Don't pick it up here.\n\nPattern worth knowing before you write your own checks: four acceptance criteria in this epic\nso far (35bc AC1/AC3, 2aa6 AC1/AC3) were blanket string prohibitions that collided with their\nown deliberate exclusions, each needing a mid-implementation amendment and a re-review. If\nyour AC contains an absolute \"returns no matches\", check it against the exclusions first.","timestamp":1785018744333402001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pre-change evidence before any implementation edit: gold set contains 30 cases (6 each across CROSS_SIBLING, DELIVERED_FUNC, DROP, FORCE_CLOSED, SECURITY_CONTRACT), with 6 expected drops and 24 expected preserves; test_completion_floor_e2e.py passes 7/7. RED-first oracle: happy, multi-epic edge, and real-store persistence tests all fail on the intended assertion because generated descriptions contain the duplicate  heading.","timestamp":1785266124001653001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Post-change operator attestation: gold-set tally remains exactly 30 total, 6 per category, 6 expected drops, 24 expected preserves; completion-floor E2E remains 7/7. TDD evidence: implementer saw only the happy-path RED test and passed it in one attempt. Restored held-out multi-epic edge and real-store persistence tests; full oracle passed. Mutation check reintroduced duplicate : both held-out tests failed on the intended heading assertion, then passed after restoration. Current focused set: 18 passed.","timestamp":1785266296016863001}],"created_at":1784944750923535001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b1a5c7ab-005f-4c3e-9207-3dec4dc49e0b","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2aa6-726a-ea56-4d6c"}],"description":"## Why\n\nThe eval specs and gold-set expectations assert against criterion PROMPT text. Once the\nreviewer prompts drop SC vocabulary, any spec still phrased in SC terms is describing a rubric\nthat no longer exists, and the eval solver actively MANUFACTURES the dual vocabulary into every\nfixture ticket it generates — reintroducing the heading the migration is removing.\n\n## What\n\nUpdate the eval specs, the eval solver's generated fixture descriptions, and the gold-set\nexpectation strings to the collapsed vocabulary.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-container.eval.yaml:6,91,93,205`\n- `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-g7.eval.yaml:36`\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py:317` — currently emits\n  `\"## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] {etext}\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n- {etext}\"`, i.e. every\n  generated fixture carries both headings with duplicated text.\n- `tests/unit/gold_set_completion.py:101,382` — expectation strings\n  (\"del-b's success criteria could be sized into two tasks\", \"fc1's success criteria could be split\").\n\n## Approach\n\nSpecs and gold-set strings are straight vocabulary edits. `eval_solver.py:317` drops the\ntrailing `## Success Criteria` block entirely rather than renaming it — the two blocks carried\nthe SAME `{etext}`, so emitting both under one heading would duplicate every criterion.\n\nThe gold-set strings are EXPECTATIONS, not inputs: changing them changes what the gold set\nscores. They are edited only because the underlying rubric wording changed, and the story\nverifies the gold set still scores as before rather than assuming it.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pytest tests/unit/gold_set_completion.py tests/unit -k \"eval or gold\"` green.\n- Confirm the gold-set pass/fail tallies are UNCHANGED versus the pre-change baseline, proving\n  the edits were vocabulary-only and did not move any expectation.\n- Assert a solver-generated fixture description now contains exactly one criteria heading.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `grep -rniE \"success[ _-]criteri(a|on)\" src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/ src/rebar/llm/evals/` returns no matches.\n- [ ] `grep -n \"success criteria\" tests/unit/gold_set_completion.py` returns no matches.\n- [ ] A solver-generated fixture description contains `## Acceptance Criteria` exactly once and\n      no `## Success Criteria`, asserted by a test over `eval_solver`'s output.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The gold-set score tally is identical to the pre-change baseline (recorded in a ticket\n      comment before the edit, compared after).\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and the full pytest suite pass.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-container.eval.yaml","reason":"Spec vocabulary"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-g7.eval.yaml","reason":"Spec vocabulary"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py","reason":"Stop emitting a duplicate SC block into generated fixtures"},{"path":"tests/unit/gold_set_completion.py","reason":"Gold-set expectation strings"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","2aa6-726a-ea56-4d6c"],["parent","1386-5e7c-391d-4a74"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"1386-5e7c-391d-4a74","parent_status_uuid":"ad946893-7aa1-408b-9fdc-0ae20b4273fa","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["vocabulary","plan-review"],"ticket_id":"93d0-adbb-f982-4d39","ticket_type":"story","title":"Update eval specs, eval solver fixtures and gold-set expectations to the collapsed vocabulary","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["719a7778-48d0-4d96-a359-0ff9c8f05334","b1a5c7ab-005f-4c3e-9207-3dec4dc49e0b","bfd9ecec-8b7b-4ee0-86a3-33146eb29ee9","1ed4be17-829f-4e65-aa36-8312646a75ac","8c97fcab-1eac-46a5-8064-88ca21734fb5","4bb344de-4002-4b46-821f-8991f5419308","a3df3dc5-9f15-4ad6-8977-bcd5d7e7c284","85a73713-bed8-49fc-b42f-10cfb2145315","b8f5b0ad-f80f-450b-8470-4de52f9646ca","ad946893-7aa1-408b-9fdc-0ae20b4273fa","022678ae-b931-4ff3-b372-fd7bce142002","a2b9764c-5df2-4853-8555-09a941baac3e","672ca4d2-902f-4759-bcba-58128016387f","ca3e47f0-9aa7-430c-aa07-9e4f635a4522"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785266296016863002,"uuid":"0a433ed9-c6e0-495a-b341-efd1ec54a9bb"}